# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Particle event R1_DISTPAR0047, 300 s, in 2 pieces (one component each) built at the attitude of their
# time span (yaw change <= 10 deg per piece); together they make up the event.

# Piece 1 of 2: 0-225.869 s after the event start.
# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/200 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 18 deg Earth-central angle (2141 km away, zenith 113.2 deg,
# azimuth 90 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 3.6e+05 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.287 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 69.28 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R1_DISTPAR0047_p1
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.ParticleType 1
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.Beam FarFieldGaussian 111.398 348.334 4.014
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.Spectrum File R1_DISTPAR0047_p1_spectrum.dat
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.Flux 0.101123
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835969910.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curves (absolute unix times): R1_DISTPAR0047_p1_lightcurve.dat, R1_DISTPAR0047_p2_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.Lightcurve File false R1_DISTPAR0047_p1_lightcurve_shifted.dat
R1_DISTPAR0047_p1.EarthOccultation false

# Piece 2 of 2: 225.869-300 s after the event start.
# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/200 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 18 deg Earth-central angle (2141 km away, zenith 113.2 deg,
# azimuth 90 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 3.6e+05 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.287 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 60.14 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R1_DISTPAR0047_p2
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.ParticleType 1
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.Beam FarFieldGaussian 111.398 339.194 4.014
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.Spectrum File R1_DISTPAR0047_p2_spectrum.dat
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.Flux 0.0133986
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.Lightcurve File false R1_DISTPAR0047_p2_lightcurve_shifted.dat
R1_DISTPAR0047_p2.EarthOccultation false
